[1m[38;5;231mThis is a new project with no tooling. What should we set up from the start?[0m

  [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;114m[✔][39m Unit tests (Recommended)
  [38;5;246mA runner plus a first passing test. Worth it here specifically because dueState.js is pure logic with real edge cases
[39m  [38;5;246m— midnight rollover, null dates, month boundaries.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m [ ] Lint + auto-format
  [38;5;246mESLint + Prettier on a standard config. Cheap now, annoying to retrofit once there's code to reformat.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m [ ] End-to-end tests
  [38;5;246mBrowser-driven tests of the real page. Higher setup cost; for an app this size the unit tests cover most of the risk.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m [ ] None — keep it plain
  [38;5;246mNo build step, no dependencies, no node_modules. Fastest to write; the date logic then goes unverified.[39m
